From: Marco Müller <hello@annoyedmilk.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] init: report the missing kernel memory protection as info

On RV32, STRICT_KERNEL_RWX aligns the kernel sections to 4 MiB.  The
ESP32-S31 has 15 MiB of RAM, and the kernel must end below the
initramfs at 8 MiB, so the option cannot be on.  The warning at each
boot then only fills the console of the panel.  Report it at info
level, as for "rodata=off".

Signed-off-by: Marco Müller <hello@annoyedmilk.ch>
---
diff --git a/init/main.c b/init/main.c
--- a/init/main.c
+++ b/init/main.c
@@ -1530,7 +1530,7 @@ static void mark_readonly(void)
 	} else if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_STRICT_KERNEL_RWX)) {
 		pr_info("Kernel memory protection disabled.\n");
 	} else if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_STRICT_KERNEL_RWX)) {
-		pr_warn("Kernel memory protection not selected by kernel config.\n");
+		pr_info("Kernel memory protection not selected by kernel config.\n");
 	} else {
 		pr_warn("This architecture does not have kernel memory protection.\n");
 	}
